course: dictionary
lesson: 71
title: Acquaintance: someone you know a little
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: An acquaintance is a person you know a little, but who is not a close friend. «She is an acquaintance from my swimming club, not a best friend.» You would say hello to her, but you would not tell her your secrets.
explain: The word can also mean knowledge of something. «I have some acquaintance with French» means I know a little French, not that I speak it perfectly. Clue words like "some" and "a little" tell you the knowledge is small.
explain: In formal speech, the word sounds grander. «Make his acquaintance» means meet him. A phrase like «a nodding acquaintance» means you know someone or something only slightly, enough to nod hello.
fact: Acquaintance is a noun. Its plural is acquaintances.
fact: An acquaintance is someone you know a bit; a close friend knows you and cares about you deeply.
fact: «An old acquaintance» means someone you have known for a long time, but not closely.
fact: «Make someone's acquaintance» is a formal way of saying meet someone.
fact: «A nodding acquaintance» means knowing someone or something only slightly.
exercise: «An acquaintance is someone you know a bit; a close friend knows you and cares about you deeply.» Which one is an acquaintance? | Your own brother or sister | A stranger you have never seen before | Your best friend since you were born | *Someone you say hello to but do not confide in
exercise: Priya says, «I have some acquaintance with French.» What does acquaintance mean here? | Fluent French with no mistakes | A French friend who lives next door | *Some knowledge of French | A French car
exercise: Which phrase means meet someone, in a formal way? | a close friend | an old friend | *make someone's acquaintance | a nodding acquaintance
test: Tom says, «She is only a nodding acquaintance.» What does he mean? | She lives in his house | She is his best friend | She is his sister | *He knows her only slightly
test: Which is the plural of acquaintance? | *acquaintances | acquaintancies | acquaintance's | acquaintanceses
exam: Which sentence uses acquaintance correctly? | We acquaintance every Tuesday at the park | I have an acquaintance with my best friend, who knows all my secrets | *I have an acquaintance from the library, whom I greet but do not know well | Acquaintance is a colour of the sea
